# .dockerignore — what never enters the build context.
#
# The build context is uploaded to the daemon in full before the first instruction runs,
# so an unignored .git directory is not a tidiness problem: it is seconds added to every
# build and, more importantly, credentials and history inside the layer cache. This file
# is a security control before it is a performance one.

# --- version control -------------------------------------------------------------------
# .git carries the full history including anything ever committed and later removed. It
# must never be in an image layer.
.git
.git*
!.gitignore
.github

# --- build output --------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
dist/
build/
out/
*.exe
*.test
*.out
*.prof
coverage*
.loadtest/
evidence/

# --- local development state -----------------------------------------------------------
# A stray .env is the most common way a real credential reaches an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
!testdata/**/*.pem

.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform.lock.hcl

# --- editors and OS ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- things the build does not need ------------------------------------------------------
# Excluded to keep the context small. Note what is NOT excluded: migrations/ and api/ stay,
# because migrations are embedded (migrations/embed.go) and the OpenAPI document is served
# by the control plane.
docs/
deploy/
helm/
terraform/
deployments/
tests/load/
tests/chaos/
tests/e2e/
*.md
!README.md
LICENSE

# Test sources are excluded from the image build but NOT from the module: `go build` never
# compiles _test.go files, so removing them shrinks the context without changing the
# binary. testdata/ goes with them.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/

# --- container tooling itself ---------------------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml

# --- caches ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
vendor/
